. 1.4x mixes in other labs' historical frontier trend, which was faster while Anthropic lagged in 2025, so it lowers the apparent jump. \n\nFor Anthropic-specific acceleration the 1.9x is", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2118468133702779169"}, {"author_id": "2115497882585645056", "conversation_id": "2118455315914187151", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:18:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118467997782462833"], "id": "2118467997782462833", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 74, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@testingcatalog @grok METR says 1.9x for Anthropic, but 1.4x when all labs' models are included. Which one is the fair comparison?", "url": "https://x.com/kiteze2x/status/2118467997782462833"}, {"author_id": "1367005670868885506", "conversation_id": "2118455315914187151", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:16:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118467476740857971"], "id": "2118467476740857971", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 55, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@testingcatalog Calling Opus 5.5 non frontier on their chart is crazy 🫣", "url": "https://x.com/Strongin_/status/2118467476740857971"}, {"author_id": "1721496460053635072", "conversation_id": "2118455315914187151", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:13:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118466843107344500"], "id": "2118466843107344500", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 26, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@testingcatalog Accelerated 1.9x since October 2025.\nOpus 5.5 already sits in the non-frontier column of their own chart.", "url": "https://x.com/buildsinews/status/2118466843107344500"}, {"author_id": "1522646229611515904", "conversation_id": "2118455315914187151", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:09:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118465785404522817"], "id": "2118465785404522817", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 124, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@testingcatalog Weren’t they the ones that said they were going to slow Ai?", "url": "https://x.com/AceroKamil/status/2118465785404522817"}, {"author_id": "2088718703026221056", "conversation_id": "2118455315914187151", "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:55:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118462286964617269"], "id": "2118462286964617269", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 85, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@testingcatalog 1.9x in a year is wild. wonder how much of that is actually AI", "url": "https://x.com/realivann/status/2118462286964617269"}, {"author_id": "417508671", "conversation_id": "2118455315914187151", "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:50:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118460991067582923"], "id": "2118460991067582923", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 56, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@testingcatalog That reported 1.9× speedup is exciting; if each generation improves the SI tools researchers use to build its successor, the gains could compound", "url": "https://x.com/thesimaximalist/status/2118460991067582923"}, {"author_id": "2105324415525191680", "conversation_id": "2118455315914187151", "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:50:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118460922767523917"], "id": "2118460922767523917", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 70, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@testingcatalog If Opus 5.5 is already “non-frontier” inside Anthropic, how far behind is the version the rest of us get to build with for free?", "url": "https://x.com/sleewppi/status/2118460922767523917"}, {"author_id": "95673344", "conversation_id": "2118455315914187151", "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:45:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118459590547509652"], "id": "2118459590547509652", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 15, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@testingcatalog the small print on their chart is doing a lot of work. it's benchmark scores growing 1.9x faster (range 1.5 to 2.8) and METR itself says it's unclear how that maps to real capability", "url": "https://x.com/nikoraus/status/2118459590547509652"}, {"author_id": "1665675488604434434", "conversation_id": "2118455315914187151", "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:44:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118459545580146908"], "id": "2118459545580146908", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 221, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@testingcatalog 15 a year to 29 a year. that's the number i'd stare at", "url": "https://x.com/amybuildsAI/status/2118459545580146908"}, {"author_id": "1404099729525559301", "conversation_id": "2118455315914187151", "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:40:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118458341479329835"], "id": "2118458341479329835", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 213, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@testingcatalog 1.9x on what metric tho", "url": "https://x.com/Chahatusharma/status/2118458341479329835"}, {"author_id": "2083862847231062016", "conversation_id": "2118455315914187151", "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:38:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118457875819598199"], "id": "2118457875819598199", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 267, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@testingcatalog Opus 5.5 finding out from a METR chart that it's the old model. Brutal.", "url": "https://x.com/Moretti_ale90/status/2118457875819598199"}, {"author_id": "49938909", "conversat